WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.534
-Justin Thomas,
It is great to see you.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.334
Welcome to the show.
-Thank you.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:06.067
-I have to mention something
because I was

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:07.968
looking at you before the show.

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:11.334
And you have a giant scrape
on your face there.

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:12.501
-Yeah.
-Can we zoom in?

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.334
Can we see that in camera
three maybe or four?

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:15.634
Yeah.
-Yeah, I got a little --

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:17.634
-So I thought maybe you just got
in a fight or something,

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:20.834
you know, as golfers do.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:23.167
You went out there and just
scrapped with somebody.

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.667
And you did.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:28.501
No, it was an intense battle
on the golf course, and --

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:31.601
-Yeah.
-It actually wasn't that.

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:34.267
-What was the name of this guy
that attacked you?

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.734
-This is Dale.

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:38.701
[ Audience aws ]
-Yeah, Dale.

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:41.033
-This was before he attacked me,
for the record.

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:44.334
-So he gave you a kiss first
and then he attacked you.

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:46.167
-Yes.
-That brutal beast, Dale.

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:47.200
-I mean, look at him.
He's a monster.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.400
-Looks like a tough guy.
Yeah, absolutely.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.100
Who is Dale to you?

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.167
-So, it's my fiancé's
maid of honor.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:56.734
We were in Chicago this past
weekend and we stayed at

00:00:56.734 --> 00:01:00.234
their house, and woke up in
the morning and Dale was there

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:02.601
and greeted us while we were
in bed, and...

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:04.767
-There you go.
-This is what happened.

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:06.601
-I want to congratulate you,
by the way.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:09.400
Last week you played in the
Presidents Cup on Team USA,

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.834
and you guys won.

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:12.100
Come on!
That's how you do it.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:15.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:01:15.968 --> 00:01:18.901
-It's got to be exciting.
That's a big moment right there.

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:20.701
-Oh, yeah.
-I know Jordan Spieth,

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:23.434
your buddy, you won with him.

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:26.434
You're best friends?
-That's what the media says.

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:27.934
Yeah, I guess we're gonna buy
into that.

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:31.234
-Yeah, I'll buy into it.
But you guys played together.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:34.501
Are you competitive still?
Or you go, now we're teammates?

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:38.133
-Well, I guess in that
situation, no, we're teammates.

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:41.601
It's nice because I've been
playing with him for so long

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:44.067
and watching his game,
I know what he's capable of.

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:47.100
And it's really nice to be
rooting for him as opposed to

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.067
not rooting against him,
but maybe not rooting

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:50.968
for him like I do normally.

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:53.901
-As best friends would do.
Yeah, as friends would do, yeah.

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:55.534
-So, I guess,
yes, we are competitive.

00:01:55.534 --> 00:01:57.300
-Yeah, I think so, too.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.234
You did something I thought was
pretty cool on Instagram.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:03.534
You posted your goals
for the year.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:05.334
And take a look at these.

00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:07.367
Why do you post this
out to the public?

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:08.701
To put more pressure on you?

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:09.968
-I don't know.
It's something I've done.

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:14.334
I've always felt like I've liked
making goals and just --

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.734
you know, I have some that are
more achievable than others

00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:17.901
and I have some
that are more difficult.

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.434
But I make everybody on my team
do it.

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:21.834
So my caddie will do it. My dad,
who's my coach, will do it.

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:23.467
My putting coach will do it.

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:25.534
You know, I'll do some stuff
with my trainer.

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:28.067
Because then --
And then I make everybody

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:30.801
share it with each other,
so everybody's held accountable.

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:33.601
And I think it's -- when I go
back to it at the end of the

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:37.367
year, I'm able to, you know, see
what I did, what I didn't do.

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:40.300
And then if somebody on my team
says that they were going to do

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:43.334
something in their goals and
they don't do it,

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:44.734
well, they're the one
that wrote their own goal,

00:02:44.734 --> 00:02:46.234
so I'm able to get on them
a little bit.

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:47.834
-Hey, come on.
-Yeah.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.534
-How is it having your dad be

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:51.067
that close to you
with your career?

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:52.334
-It's great. It's great.

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:54.801
We have an unbelievable
relationship.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:57.868
I think we've done a really good
job over the past, you know,

00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:01.834
handful of years of -- well,
one was probably me maturing.

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:04.701
Maybe my stubbornness got
out of the way a little bit.

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.701
-Every kid does.
-Exactly.

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:10.501
Just separating the father/son
and player/coach, you know.

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:12.167
We know that when we're at
the golf course,

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:15.601
we're there for business
and when we're away from

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:18.133
the golf course, he's my dad
and one of my best friends.

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:19.601
So I'm very, very lucky
to have him.

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:21.801
-What does your dad do
when you do something bad?

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.534
Does he look at you
and go like...?

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:25.701
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:30.934
-I remember playing baseball and
eventually I felt bad for my dad

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:34.167
because I was so bad
and all the dads kept giving

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.100
my dad advice on
how to make me better.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.267
I was like, "Dad, you don't have
to come anymore."

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:40.067
-Look at you now.
-Look at me.

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:41.734
-One of the best baseball
players in the world.

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:43.467
I mean, thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.467 --> 00:03:45.100
We're like twins.
-Yeah.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.033
-But it must be interesting.

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:49.567
Even as a dad to go like,
you got to make your moves.

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:51.901
Sometimes I'm more coach.
Sometimes I'm more dad.

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:55.367
And, like, how much pressure
do you put on your son?

00:03:55.367 --> 00:04:00.434
-I mean, he is great because I
think my grandpa was pretty hard

00:04:00.434 --> 00:04:04.667
on him, so he understands that
he didn't like that.

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:06.033
So he knew not to do it to me.

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:07.434
-Too much.
-Exactly.

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:09.234
So I'm very, very lucky,
like I said.

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:11.467
We have a great relationship.
And he's, I would say,

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:14.667
the opposite of -- sometimes I
would like him to be harder

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:19.934
on me because he feels like he
doesn't want to interfere.

00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:21.868
He doesn't want to say something
that would mess me up.

00:04:21.868 --> 00:04:24.934
But we've -- Not arguments,
but we've had these

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:26.267
conversations many times.

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:28.534
I'm like, "Dad, we're out here.
You're my coach.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.567
You're not my dad.
You're out here to make me

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:33.200
better at golf, and that's what
you need to do."

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:34.434
-I love that.

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:38.100
I was recently golfing with
Justin Timberlake.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.634
-The other J.T.
-Yeah.

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:42.534
The other J.T.?
-Yeah.

00:04:42.534 --> 00:04:44.667
-I guess he can go by that,
yeah, the other J.T.

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:45.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.834 --> 00:04:47.467
But, you know, serious,
serious game.

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:49.434
I take it very seriously.
I was out there with

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:53.000
Travis Kelce and Patrick
Mahomes, and I had a shot

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.868
out of the bunker in the sand.

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:56.501
A lot of pressure.
-I think I saw that.

00:04:56.501 --> 00:04:58.367
-Well, if you missed it,
we have it right here.

00:04:58.367 --> 00:04:59.534
-Yeah.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:04.667
-Oh! Go in! Go in!

00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:06.067
-Oh!

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:07.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:10.734 --> 00:05:13.734
-I mean, no big deal.
No big deal right there.

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:15.767
You saw it.

00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:18.334
I know you wanted
some tips from me.

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:20.200
All that stuff.
We'll get to that later.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.033
You know, I'll talk to your dad.
We'll figure it out.

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:25.868
-I think one of my favorite
parts about that video is,

00:05:25.868 --> 00:05:28.934
you always hear the --
when people maybe overreact --

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:30.367
not saying that
that was overreacting.

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:33.234
But the whole --
-That was overreacting?

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:35.734
-Like act like you've been
there, and it was very clear

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:37.467
that you had never been there
in that moment.

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:40.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:42.367
But I love it. It was great.
-That's so funny.

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:44.467
-It was great.
-That is so funny.

00:05:44.467 --> 00:05:46.400
You're right.
I've never been there.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.367
[ Laughter ]
-Sorry, sorry.

00:05:48.367 --> 00:05:50.701
-While you've been competing
recently,

00:05:50.701 --> 00:05:52.434
I know that you've been followed
by a film crew.

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:55.100
They're doing a documentary
coming out next year on Netflix.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.534
-Yeah.
-Do you get nervous when

00:05:56.534 --> 00:05:59.033
the camera is always on you or
are you just used to it now?

00:05:59.033 --> 00:06:01.200
-I think, and to be perfectly
honest, in a situation

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.534
like this, I'm a little more
nervous with a film crew

00:06:03.534 --> 00:06:05.501
because this is not
my comfort zone.

00:06:05.501 --> 00:06:07.501
When I'm on a golf course,
that's what I do.

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:10.067
So I'm very comfortable
in that atmosphere.

00:06:10.067 --> 00:06:12.200
But I think it's going to
be great.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.801
It's going to be on Netflix
early 2023.

00:06:14.801 --> 00:06:18.567
It's just going to give,
first off, a lot of people

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:21.167
outside of golf to take a look
at inside of golfers' lives.

00:06:21.167 --> 00:06:23.501
But just see more of
the day-to-day.

00:06:23.501 --> 00:06:25.968
I mean, they had moments where
they're in the car with me

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:28.267
driving to the golf course, or
they're watching me workout,

00:06:28.267 --> 00:06:30.567
or they're having dinner with
some guys, whatever it is.

00:06:30.567 --> 00:06:33.334
And I think it's going to
be a really cool thing

00:06:33.334 --> 00:06:34.767
for people to see.

00:06:34.767 --> 00:06:37.200
-You do this thing,
it's like your signature move.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.033
After you take a shot,
you twirl your club.

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:41.267
And it's almost like, to me,
like a mike drop.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:43.167
And I have a couple clubs here.
-Okay.

00:06:43.167 --> 00:06:44.801
-I was just wondering if you
could just teach me how to do it

00:06:44.801 --> 00:06:46.534
and just do it on
"The Tonight Show"?

00:06:46.534 --> 00:06:49.734
-Yeah, I'd love to.

00:06:49.734 --> 00:06:51.300
Where would you like to face?

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.534
Are we hitting this way?

00:06:52.534 --> 00:06:54.133
-No, hit to the audience, right?

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:57.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:06:57.968 --> 00:07:00.501
So, I mean, we don't need to
take the full swing obviously.

00:07:00.501 --> 00:07:02.667
But it's like, you know, you
follow through -- I want to make

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:04.067
sure I don't hit anything
up here.

00:07:04.067 --> 00:07:05.834
-Yep.
-And then, you can kind of --

00:07:05.834 --> 00:07:08.501
it depends on if you're left-
or right-hand dominant.

00:07:08.501 --> 00:07:11.334
I think Tiger likes to go right
because then you can kind of

00:07:11.334 --> 00:07:14.667
get the little -- you can get
the hand in there.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:17.267
That was good. That was great.
That was awesome.

00:07:17.267 --> 00:07:20.267
Or you know you can go left
and just -- it's just kind of

00:07:20.267 --> 00:07:24.033
the swagger sometimes that
golfers can attempt to have.

00:07:24.033 --> 00:07:25.968
I know we don't have a lot.
-No, I can try.

00:07:25.968 --> 00:07:29.133
So, just up, follow through --
-It's just kind of natural.

00:07:29.133 --> 00:07:31.300
You're following through,
and then just --

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.634
-And then spin it.
[ Cheers ]

00:07:33.634 --> 00:07:35.133
Like that?
-That's good enough.

00:07:35.133 --> 00:07:36.767
-Let's do it together. Ready?
-Alright.

00:07:36.767 --> 00:07:38.267
-One -- Wait.

00:07:38.267 --> 00:07:40.067
Two should be here, right?

00:07:40.067 --> 00:07:41.534
-What's that?
Oh, so we're like --

00:07:41.534 --> 00:07:43.334
-Oh, maybe this.
-Are we back to --

00:07:43.334 --> 00:07:45.701
-No, now we're in a movie.
We're in a buddy cop movie.

00:07:45.701 --> 00:07:47.801
Alright.
On two we'll be up here.

00:07:47.801 --> 00:07:49.634
-Okay.
-So we need to be --

00:07:49.634 --> 00:07:51.033
-So it's up on one?
-Yeah.

00:07:51.033 --> 00:07:52.067
-Okay.

00:07:52.067 --> 00:07:56.000
-One, two, three.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:58.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:58.067 --> 00:07:59.534
-Justin Thomas.

00:07:59.534 --> 00:08:01.601
Check him out on the PGA Tour
this season.

00:08:01.601 --> 00:08:04.501
We'll be right back with
a performance from Sam Hunt.

00:08:04.501 --> 00:08:05.968
Stick around, everybody!

